hone calls and  the struggle financially to try and keep  supporting  him in prison was just too much for her  rafferty's relative hopes sharing their  story will reopen the conversation about  rafferty's move to medium security  in solidarity with tory stafford's  family to know that his family  is willing to make those steps as well  to  do what's right in this case it's i  couldn't i couldn't appreciate it  anymore  mark carcassel global news toronto  barriers to vaccination still ahead the  essential workers who  may not get their shots  you're watching global national  one of the most important tools to  protect people against kova 19  is the vaccine as provinces ramp up  their rollouts advocates are raising  concerns about some essential workers  being excluded  because of their immigration status  there are about 1.6 million migrants  refugees  and undocumented people in canada many  of them are in industries at high risk  of exposure working long hours  with low pay but as christa hessie  reports  they're facing huge barriers to get  vaccinated  lily has risked her life working on the  front lines in one of the most dangerous  settings for covet 19 deaths in the  country  long-term care homes she should have  been one of the first people to receive  the vaccine  we are on the front lines every day like  everybody else and still we are being  bored  still in january lily's employer sent an  email asking staff for their provincial  health card in order to get it  something she does not have we're not  using her real name  she's undocumented and she fears she  could be deported  it's something that plays on your mind  every single day that you could be found  out  despite assurances from federal and  provincial governments that the vaccine  will be available to everyone  regardless of status advocates say the  reality on the ground is quite different  even though provinces have laws  governing consent and the sharing of  health data  for undocumented people the fear of  personal information being shared with  border services  and possible deportation is too great  karen koch from the migrant rights  network says they're already seeing  people struggle with access  so unless those concrete measures are  taken to ensure  in practice that everyone has access the  policy won't matter  this deeply ingrained fear could mean  the half a million undocumented people  in canada  don't receive vaccines if you don't  treat  everyone in your community and it's a  pandemic  you treat no one everyone is at risk  global news reached out to the  ministries of health in ontario british  columbia and quebec  provinces that have large numbers of  migrants and undocumented people  all provinces said a health card will  not be required to get the vaccine  but they do require information such as  a full name date of birth and address  that level of identification would keep  them away the migrant rights network  says granting people permanent status  would solve a lot of these problems  permanent residency is what's going to  give people access to the same rights  and protections as everybody else  colford says he's frustrated by the lack  of action from the federal government  after all these years they still  continue  to let these people fend for themselves  and be lost  christa hessie global news tomorrow on  the new reality  krista will take a deeper look at the  medical volunteers trying to provide  care for undocumented patients  turned away from hospital or told to pay  for treatment  that's saturday night at 7 pm right here  on global  up next the canadians putting retirement  on hold to help out  on the front lines  some canadians are putting retirement on  pause to join the fight against coven  19.  thousands of doctors nurses and other  health professionals have already spent  long careers  caring for the sick and will now serve  as critical reinforcements  for canada's mass immunization effort  karen lieberman shares their stories  as vaccine supply ramps up across the  country the number of vaccination  clinics is growing i do need permission  to give you this vaccine can i have your  consent  please heeding the call to help you can  retire but you can never stop being a  nurse  a not so fresh crop of health  professionals  rejoining the workforce  45 years in nursing was not enough for  lorraine gonzalez  she now spends 12 hours a day at this  vaccine clinic  i just felt that i had something more to  give so when they said  can you come back and vaccinate i  thought yes  returning as a reinforcement on the  front line was a no-brainer for this  general surgeon  it's extremely satisfying particularly  the patient population we're dealing  with now in the over 80s  these are remarkable people even though  he only  just retired three months ago it didn't  work out so well did it  no last spring the registered nurses  association of ontario reached out to  past  members we acted right away with the  nurse and we got i think  over 10 000 nurses not all retired  that were willing to go to icu to  vaccinations to do to  case and contact tracing you name it you  still got to wash your hands  jane cornelius a former icu manager has  come out of retirement  twice in april they asked me to come  back and help  and then i went back into retirement  because things settled down  and now with vaccination they've asked  us to come back and help  common among these retirees is their  eagerness to pitch in  people needed help and that's what  family doctors do is they jump in there  and help whenever help is needed  the way out of this pandemic she says is  to get everybody vaccinated  until then retirement is put on pause  i'm hoping by september that i'm flying  off somewhere nice and warm  time on the golf course the the things  you should be doing when you're retired  karen lieberman global news toronto  and that is global national for this  friday night i'm robin gill  tonight your canada is a view of the  portman bridge from coquitlam bc  we'd love to see your corner of this  country so please keep sending your  photos  to viewers at globalnational.com thank  you for watching and i'll see you back  here tomorrow have a great night
 

